{"posts":[{"id":"pg_p1_1","t":"Hi Friends, I went through all the materials I found here in RTM, whether it is Marketpedia, Homework section or Journals, I found all of them to be extremely important and simple to learn, nevertheless to say, this is a Gem of a Community, where all the members are actively participating, sharing and learning together.\n\nWell I believe, \"Knowledge is the only thing, that increases by sharing\". And happy to see that happening here, time and again.\n\nAnd this is what is knocking in my head, to open my own \"Journal\" to carry on with the spirit of \"Learning by sharing\". So henceforth, I will post here, all the analysis I do or whatever doubts I have or something new which I come across, in terms of RTM style of Trading and Psychology.\n\nAnd one request, please do pardon my bad English, as my Mother Language is Bengali.\n\nThanks and Regards, Prosenjit (PG)","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#1","p":1,"im":[],"m":1},{"id":"pg_p1_2","t":"Working on Decision Points, SR's, Engulfs and FTR's. Trying to discriminate the difference between FTR and a reaction (DBR) in a Flag Area.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#2","p":1,"im":["34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592"],"m":2},{"id":"pg_p1_3","t":"Trying to confluence RTM strategies with Investment strategies in Indian Index (Nifty) and trying to forecast it's future direction.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#3","p":1,"im":["f1d3ebe03a2aa9938f0d17c8174632b60c491951"],"m":3},{"id":"pg_p1_4","t":"When we identify a Quasimodo in a Monthly chart, the trade is going to be a SET and FORGET one for sure. I took this trade in Options but closed it a little early because of my emotional effects. Seems need to manage emotions in a better way.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#4","p":1,"im":["7aaf4cf6c55a0f79089f6fabcd49d9d8812629a8"],"m":4},{"id":"pg_p1_5","t":"prosenjitghosh wrote: Working on Decision Points, SR's, Engulfs and FTR's. Trying to discriminate the difference between FTR and a reaction (DBR) in a Flag Area.\n\nNot bad. a bit time and you see your mistakes. I don't want to make corrections.. I see you soon correct these mistakes.","a":"Kovalenko","d":"","n":"#5","p":1,"im":["34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592"],"m":5},{"id":"pg_p1_6","t":"Thank you very much for your feedback, shall surely try to find out my mistakes.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#6","p":1,"im":[],"m":6},{"id":"pg_p1_7","t":"Working on PAZ, CP PAZ, FTR and FL","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#7","p":1,"im":["fc436d6a7dfee4070101f45086d5c56a2e46e210"],"m":7},{"id":"pg_p1_8","t":"Well I have rectified the mistakes, hope this time I have made it correct...","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#8","p":1,"im":["6352960087aee7c2ae8cd678c1e760e4c433882a"],"m":8},{"id":"pg_p1_9","t":"Spotted another Diamond today...","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#9","p":1,"im":["16c0f837d64ada663716b4436ffd48e5e18de60d"],"m":9},{"id":"pg_p1_10","t":"Liquidity Spike to a True Supply after Compression.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#10","p":1,"im":["da2731109e4e8b7e325082038e69ef92c5067512"],"m":10},{"id":"pg_p1_11","t":"Yeah nice, these are very good opportunities... Price struggles to move up then suddenly explodes upwards into supply. Very high probability fakeout.:) Well done.","a":"ZeeDeveel","d":"","n":"#11","p":1,"im":[],"m":11},{"id":"pg_p1_12","t":"Reading a session","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#12","p":1,"im":["81b20efcf485f542f1befb1a88c37d07ec5be70c"],"m":12},{"id":"pg_p1_13","t":"Engulf (1) will be FO, bcoz (4) Engulfed ( i.e after (4) engulf formation, (1) becomes FO)","a":"praveenignite","d":"","n":"#13","p":1,"im":[],"m":13},{"id":"pg_p1_14","t":"The trade went exactly as per plan, only missed out in the long trade. That pivot in a Lower Time Frame is a FTR. And look how it worked as a Bear Trap. Shall keep a watch on such things next time.\n\nIn LTF the pivot looks like a FTR and it reacted so well.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#14","p":1,"im":["6aab508cf1387a5c9e19cb4713567a1776004e00","dc2f4f32f0b8204e61a9e686cc0c503bfece6e4e"],"m":14},{"id":"pg_p1_15","t":"Crude trade, got full target","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#15","p":1,"im":["e707eddf4b8dfe65b2a7ddf60e655732aa3beeca"],"m":15},{"id":"pg_p1_16","t":"Hi\n\nAfter you've done your analysis on candlestick chart, check line chart also....you wouldn't miss out any important FTRs","a":"tudor3","d":"","n":"#16","p":1,"im":[],"m":16},{"id":"pg_p1_17","t":"Like your journal posts, clear and concise. Keep it Up..!","a":"claudiuschan","d":"","n":"#17","p":1,"im":[],"m":17},{"id":"pg_p1_18","t":"I can't recommend the use of line charts at all.\n\nWe need the highs AND lows of every candle to read PA","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#18","p":1,"im":[],"m":18},{"id":"pg_p1_19","t":"Ifmyante wrote: I can't recommend the use of line charts at all.\n\nWe need the highs AND lows of every candle to read PA\n\nNoted, shall follow candlestick charts only....","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#19","p":1,"im":[],"m":19},{"id":"pg_p1_20","t":"Reading a Session, Decision Points and trying to predict future movement. Weekly Chart\n\nDaily Chart\n\n60 Minutes Chart","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#20","p":1,"im":["ac890045364092ec006914d29034b5ddcffed9f3","62ba15b7046161e92779c7b1529be0cf90c4f28f","ed331b77965911e87de442682fef8b9b78bab3f4"],"m":20},{"id":"pg_p1_21","t":"prosenjitghosh wrote: Reading a Session, Decision Points and trying to predict future movement. Weekly Chart","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#21","p":1,"im":["ac890045364092ec006914d29034b5ddcffed9f3","62ba15b7046161e92779c7b1529be0cf90c4f28f","ed331b77965911e87de442682fef8b9b78bab3f4","4fff462daf77449c839c27a70da98c143634401a"],"m":21},{"id":"pg_p1_22","t":"","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#22","p":1,"im":["c5e67b94a20011401f46a937e79f777ee6077104"],"m":22},{"id":"pg_p1_23","t":"prosenjitghosh wrote:\n\nprosenjitghosh wrote: Reading a Session, Decision Points and trying to predict future movement. Weekly Chart\n\nUpdate on the same trade. Learned something new and Read a session, decision making and Diamond. 60 Mins chart\n\nAnd today's 5 mins chart","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#23","p":1,"im":["ac890045364092ec006914d29034b5ddcffed9f3","62ba15b7046161e92779c7b1529be0cf90c4f28f","ed331b77965911e87de442682fef8b9b78bab3f4","4fff462daf77449c839c27a70da98c143634401a","2a16a27cd5f97672e20ef4c5db5ae5b2b636e8b0","55b51cac4cf47214748268eb1148f04c63abe1aa"],"m":23},{"id":"pg_p1_24","t":"The game of Compression, Liquidity Gap, SR Flip's, Fake outs and the Institutions game plan for the conventional pattern trader's.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#24","p":1,"im":["62b20a4d9fbaad5064eea575c2e6d72f08955513"],"m":24},{"id":"pg_p1_25","t":"Pending homework of \"The CANCAN\"","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#25","p":1,"im":["3afe3bfadac0f31def9df66e2cf7e79ebb79b0b8"],"m":25}],"images":[{"k":"34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592","t":"assets/thumbs/34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592.webp","f":"assets/images/34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":141327,"o":"34936f46311a010b437fb7490967a7fd7aabd592.jpeg","p":1,"pid":"pg_p1_5"},{"k":"f1d3ebe03a2aa9938f0d17c8174632b60c491951","t":"assets/thumbs/f1d3ebe03a2aa9938f0d17c8174632b60c491951.webp","f":"assets/images/f1d3ebe03a2aa9938f0d17c8174632b60c491951.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":146033,"o":"f1d3ebe03a2aa9938f0d17c8174632b60c491951.jpeg","p":1,"pid":"pg_p1_3"},{"k":"7aaf4cf6c55a0f79089f6fabcd49d9d8812629a8","t":"assets/thumbs/7aaf4cf6c55a0f79089f6fabcd49d9d8812629a8.webp","f":"assets/images/7aaf4cf6c55a0f79089f6fabcd49d9d8812629a8.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":141244,"o":"7aaf4cf6c55a0f79089f6fabcd49d9d8812629a8.jpeg","p":1,"pid":"pg_p1_4"},{"k":"fc436d6a7dfee4070101f45086d5c56a2e46e210","t":"assets/thumbs/fc436d6a7dfee4070101f45086d5c56a2e46e210.webp","f":"assets/images/fc436d6a7dfee4070101f45086d5c56a2e46e210.jpeg","w":1366,"h":738,"b":147407,"o":"fc436d6a7dfee4070101f45086d5c56a2e46e210.jpeg","p":1,"pid